@cc [owner:philipperolet,label:architecture] preserve-completed-backfills
Once a backfill has completed its intended production run, keep its source as a historical record:
do not delete it or change its implementation. The only exception is work explicitly preparing the
same backfill to run again.

If later application changes break a completed TypeScript backfill, add a top-level
`// @ts-nocheck` instead of adapting its implementation. Its dedicated test may be deleted.
